==German==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[ˈzaʊ̯ɡn̩]|lang=de}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|sugan|sūgan|to suck|lang=goh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{recons|sūganą|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{recons|sug-|lang=ine-pro}}, {{recons|suk-|lang=ine-pro}}. Compare Low German {{term|sugen|lang=nds}}, Dutch {{term|zuigen|lang=nl}}, Danish {{term|suge|lang=da}}.

====Verb====
{{de-verb-strong|class=2|saugt|sog|gesogen}}

# {{intransitive}} to [[suck]]; to create underpressure with a tube-like object such as one's mouth
#: '''''saugen''' an etwas'' — “to suck on something”
# {{transitive}} to [[suck]] (something)
# {{colloquial|lang=de}}, {{transitive}} to [[download]] something

